# Praxis issue standard (generated)

Generated by `go run ./cmd/praxis-doc` from the ebac package `internal/praxis`; do not edit by hand. A praxis issue is an entity form; GitHub shows what this package renders from it, and the gh-cache sync refuses a form this package's validator refuses.

## The form

| Key | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `praxis.topic` | the stack's topic, one line, no brackets |
| `praxis.k` | 0 for the stack's issue 0, else this piece's place 1..n |
| `praxis.n` | how many pieces the stack has (at least 1) |
| `praxis.parent` | the parent issue number (required for k >= 1) |
| `praxis.summary` | the title's text |
| `praxis.delivers` | the one-line outcome |
| `praxis.status` | one of `claimed`, `split`, `in-progress`, `pr-open`, `done` |
| `praxis.assignee` | the GitHub login that holds it |
| `praxis.prs[]` | the PRs that fix it |
| `praxis.children[]` | an issue 0's pieces (number, k, summary, status) |
| `praxis.contract` | optional: the body of its ## Contract section |

## Shapes

- Issue 0: title `[<topic>][0-<n>] <summary>`; body opens with `Delivers:` and lists its pieces under `## Stack` in k order.
- Piece: title `[<topic>][<k>-<n>] <summary>`; body opens with `Part of #<parent>`, `Stack: <k> of <n>`, `Delivers: ...`.
- Deeper tiers repeat the shape under a piece.
- A PR that fixes a piece says `Fixes #<piece>` in its body.

## Example tree

### Issue 0 title

```
[Example topic][0-2] What the whole stack delivers
```

### Issue 0 body

```
Delivers: the outcome the stack exists for

## Stack
- [1-2] #1001 First piece (in-progress)
- [2-2] #1002 Second piece (claimed)
```

### Split comment

```
**Status:** split into a stack of 2 pieces

- [1-2] #1001 First piece (in-progress)
- [2-2] #1002 Second piece (claimed)

John Kelliher's agents (figaro builder)
```

### Piece title

```
[Example topic][1-2] First piece
```

### Piece body

```
Part of #1000
Stack: 1 of 2
Delivers: one checkable outcome of this piece

## Contract
Delivers: one checkable outcome of this piece
Owner: ours
Status: building
Acceptance:
- <a statement that is red on revert>
```

### Claim comment

```
Claimed by John Kelliher's agents (figaro builder). Assignee: @ours.
```

### Status comment

```
**Status:** in-progress

John Kelliher's agents (figaro builder)
```

### Done comment

```
**Status:** done: fixed by #2001

John Kelliher's agents (figaro builder)
```

## Refusals

The sync raises `sync.alarm.praxis.<rule>` on the issue's form and posts nothing.

| Rule | Refused when |
|---|---|
| `bad_topic` | the topic is empty, has a bracket or a line break |
| `n_out_of_range` | n < 1 |
| `k_out_of_range` | k < 0 or k > n |
| `no_parent` | a piece (k >= 1) names no parent |
| `self_parent` | an issue names itself as parent |
| `parent_closed` | the parent is closed |
| `parent_done` | the parent is done |
| `empty_summary` | the summary is empty |
| `empty_delivers` | delivers is empty |
| `bad_status` | the status is not one of `claimed`, `split`, `in-progress`, `pr-open`, `done` |
| `split_without_children` | the status is split with no children |
| `child_out_of_range` | a child's k is outside 1..n |
| `done_without_prs` | done with no PRs (an issue 0 may be done when every child is done) |
